  "body": "Main is red (#4322, P1) on three suites. Each one asserts the output of a post that two merged PRs changed on purpose:\n\n| Suite | Cause | Change |\n|---|---|---|\n| post `wcs_flip_dialects` | #4196 writes `G92.1 G97` in the LinuxCNC preamble; the mirror trace model refused them (\"G92.1 is not modelled\") and `golden/wcs_flip/linuxcnc_x.nc` had the old line | model `G92.1` (clears G92 offsets; the trace models none) and `G97` (rpm mode) as no-motion codes; regenerate the golden: the diff is exactly that preamble line |\n| app `wcs_index` | #4299 raised Tormach to 500 offsets (`G54.1 P10`-`P500`) | expect `max 500`, offset 10 named `G54.1 P10`, the fallback name tested at 501; the setup command's own bound (`MAX_SLOT + 1 = 255`) still applies |\n| ui lib `setup_wcs_tests::the_combo_lists_the_setups_post_range_by_its_names` | same | the combo lists 255 entries; 7 = G59.1, 9 = G59.3, 10 = G54.1 P10 |\n\n**No product code changes.** The posted output itself is #4196's and #4299's, which were reviewed there.\n\n**How tested (macOS, debug):** `camcraft-post --test wcs_flip_dialects` 9/9, `camcraft-app --test wcs_index` 4/4, `camcraft-ui --lib setup_wcs_tests` 6/6; clippy `-D warnings` on post, app and ui (all targets) clean. These are every failing step of post-merge run 45971148860.\n\n**Not exercised:** Windows (bacon and winnie fail the same suites; `mcp_live` idle_timeout there is separate, #4252).\n\n**Note for review:** the app's setup offset bound (255) is now below Tormach's stated 500, so offsets 256-500 cannot be picked; that is a limit, not a wrong output. Filed separately if wanted.\n\nChangelog: none (tests only)\n\nFixes #4322\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
